    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "C. 1.00 ACRE DEVELOPMENT SITE, WITHIN WALKING DISTANCE OF THE TOWN CENTRE. \r\n\r\n(0.468 ACRES ZONED STRTEGIC RESIDENTIAL RESERVE)\r\n\r\nBrilliantly located along the banks of the River Camlin, adjacent to The Albert Reynolds Peace Park (The Mall), this property comprises of a c.1 acre site, in a much sought-after area of Longford Town.\r\n\r\nWithin minutes walking distance of the town centre, Longford Train station, The Cathedral, Shopping centres, as well as the Royal canal walk. This property presents a fantastic opportunity, in one of the most desired residential areas in the town.\r\n\r\nViewing highly recommended by the sole Auctioneers.\r\n\r\nPlease contact us on 043 3350555 to book your viewing.\r\n\r\nFOLIO NO. LD8628\r\n\r\nDIRECTIONS: GPS: 53.73210971210959, -7.792259420880522"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Adjacent to The Mall Complex\r\n\r\nCamlin River frontage\r\n\r\n200m to St. Mel’s College \r\n\r\nServiced with Footpath, Street lighting \r\n\r\n15-minute walk to the Train Station\r\n\r\nTrain Station: 7 Trains a day on the Dublin-Sligo Line\r\n\r\nExcellent access to N4 Dublin/Sligo and N5 Longford/Westport Routes \r\n\r\nJust 1.5 mile from the N63/R397 Roscommon/Athlone Route\r\n\r\nFibre Broadband available\r\n\r\n10 minutes to The Royal Canal Walk\r\n\r\nNote:\r\nReceipt of these particulars implies an obligation to conduct all negotiations through Padraic Davis Auctioneers LTD. The contents do not constitute an offer or form the basis of any contract. All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition etc, are given in good faith and are believed to be correct. Any intending purchasers should not rely on them and are strongly advised to view the property for themselves. All measurements are approximate, and photographs provided are for guidance purposes only. These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer; they do not form any part of a resulting contract. \r\n\r\nThe boundary markings for this land holding, outlined in Red, are strictly for guidance purposes only."
      }
    ],
